            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.087,
            0.847,
            0.143
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, the next step is multiplying this result by 5. This gives the product of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 5 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 3 } { 2 } ;"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.174,
            0.148,
            0.349,
            0.185
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_7_equation_2.jpg",
          "content": "\\frac{5}{4} \\times \\frac{3}{2} = 5 \\times \\frac{3}{8} = \\frac{15}{8}."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.205,
            0.846,
            0.249
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Connection between the Area of a Rectangle and Fraction Multiplication"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.258,
            0.847,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the Fig. 8.3, what is the length and breadth of the shaded rectangle? Since we started with a unit square (of side 1 unit), the length and"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.297,
            0.449,
            0.332
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "breadth are "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " unit and "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " unit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.339,
            0.599,
            0.432
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the area of this rectangle? We see that 8 such rectangles give the square of area 1 square unit. So, the area of each rectangle is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 8 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " square units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.609,
            0.307,
            0.833,
            0.436
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.609,
                0.307,
                0.833,
                0.436
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_7.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.433,
            0.599,
            0.473
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you see any relation between the area and the product of length and breadth?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.713,
            0.444,
            0.778,
            0.459
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig. 8.3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.483,
            0.846,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The area of a rectangle of fractional sides equals the product of its sides."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.52,
            0.847,
            0.559
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In general, if we want to find the product of two fractions, we can find the area of the rectangle formed with the two fractions as its sides."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.565,
            0.293,
            0.589
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.592,
            0.846,
            0.631
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Find the following products. Use a unit square as a whole for representing the fractions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.637,
            0.31,
            0.793
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 3 } \\times \\frac { 1 } { 5 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 4 } \\times \\frac { 1 } { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (c) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{5} \\times \\frac{1}{2}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (d) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{6} \\times \\frac{1}{5}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.796,
            0.369,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now, find "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac { 1 } { 1 2 } \\times \\frac { 1 } { 1 8 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
